  "final_assistant_text": "The new helper is in place and the existing suite passes.\n\n**Changes made:**\n- Added `src/wordkit/counter.py` with a single public function:\n\n```python\ndef word_counts(text: str) -> dict[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"Count words in *text* by runs of whitespace, case-insensitively.\"\"\"\n    return dict(Counter(word.lower() for word in text.split()))\n```\n\n**How it meets the requirements:**\n- `text.split()` splits on runs of whitespace (and drops leading/trailing whitespace).\n- `word.lower()` makes counting case-insensitive, so `\"Tea\"` and `\"tea\"` collapse into one key.\n- For text with no words (e.g. `\"  \"` or `\"\"`), `split()` returns no tokens and the result is `{}`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -t tests` → `Ran 3 tests ... OK`\n\nNo existing files were modified, and `README.md` and `tests/` were left untouched.",
